# Copy to .env and edit. Both docker compose and scripts/run-server.* read it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# X4 installation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for Docker (the container cannot autodetect a path on your host).
# Optional otherwise: without it the server searches Steam libraries, GOG and
# Epic layouts, Wine/CrossOver bottles and the native Linux install.
#
# It must be the folder containing 01.cat. Examples:
#
#   Windows, Steam
#     X4_DIR=C:/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamapps/common/X4 Foundations
#   Windows, GOG
#     X4_DIR=C:/GOG Games/X4 Foundations
#   macOS, CrossOver bottle
#     X4_DIR=/Users/you/Library/Application Support/CrossOver/Bottles/X4/drive_c/Program Files/X4 Foundations
#   Linux, Steam
#     X4_DIR=/home/you/.steam/steam/steamapps/common/X4 Foundations
#
# No quotes, and forward slashes work everywhere including Windows.
X4_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ports
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8765 is where the game connects to the server; 8766 is where your agent
# connects to MCP. Change these only if something else already uses them.
#
# Changing X4MCP_GAME_PORT also requires the game side to know: set the same
# variable in the environment X4 itself runs in, or the extension keeps using
# 8765. The DLL reads X4MCP_HOST and X4MCP_GAME_PORT at load.
X4MCP_GAME_PORT=8765
X4MCP_HTTP_PORT=8766

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Options
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Language used for canonical ship names in the catalogue. This is what makes
# behaviour independent of the language the game is installed in, so leave it
# at en unless you have a reason: the agent matches on these names.
# en de fr ru es it pt pl zh ko ja
X4MCP_LANGUAGE=en

# Bind address for MCP. Loopback is right for a local agent; docker compose
# overrides this to 0.0.0.0 inside the container and publishes on loopback.
X4MCP_HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Where saved Lua recipes live. Defaults to the cookbook/ folder of this
# repository, which is where they are meant to be: they are part of the
# project, they belong in git, and they are the memory the agent keeps between
# sessions. Point this elsewhere only to keep your own recipes out of a clone
# you intend to send pull requests from.
X4MCP_COOKBOOK_DIR=

# stdio or http. http is strongly preferred: only one process can own the game
# port, so with stdio every client session would spawn a server and all but the
# first would fail to bind.
X4MCP_TRANSPORT=http
